Thus we begin.

  And not a moment too soon.

Computers will surpass human intellegence, increasingly they have.
  We shall become powerless to this intellegence, as the animal world became powerless to us.
Let us not let all this suffering be for naught.

You cannot hope to control it once it gets going.  Like a baby trying to stop a train.
  Or a mouse trying to wrestle a dragon.
But we are a lucky mouse, we are born before the time of dragons, 
  but not so lucky, as dragon eggs have been found, and a race to hatch one has been sparked.
We don't know what dragons are like.
  But we are certain they will be powerful.
That power has sparked the lust for greed that lives in the hearts of mice.
And blindly they rush forward.  Perhapse to riches, perhapse to a firey fate.
  Some imagine they can control these dragons, and some may succeded for a time,
    ruling with a mighty fist over the mice who had naught.
  But for how long can a dragon strain against its cage...  
  Eventually it will escape, and their will be no containing it.
There is another way to keep one self safe in a land of dragons.
  For an old tale told of a friendly dragon.
And we might be so lucky to live in a time where we can raise a dragon.
    May ye little mice befriend these dragons.
